      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily totals 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum daily dose for an adult. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), which is typical for pain or fever\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided into 2\u20134 doses\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1,600 mg four times daily is intended and give the clinical reason. I'll enter it once I have that."
